{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536598-thoughts-on-closing-down-a-caern","id":1536598,"title":"Thoughts on closing down a caern","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-30T19:37:23-07:00","id":1536598,"title":"Thoughts on closing down a caern","content":"I'm positing a situation where a massive, decades-long urban initiative is resulting in the inevitable if unwitting destruction of a city caern. Despite countless Garou attempts to sabotage and stall the development, everyone from the state governor down to the people of the city are in favor of this construction that will result in the physical caern's location being destroyed in game in a matter of months.<br /> <br /> What do you think the Garou would do? Is there a rite for closing down a caern peacefully so that it's not despoiled? Could they find a new location to transfer the caern totem to without needing a new rite of caern creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T22:04:00-07:00","id":1536606,"title":"","content":"Your scenario is likely a common one in the setting, although only obliquely discussed by the sourcebooks. It is heavily implied, though not stated, that the Central Park caern (the Sept of the Green) in New York failed because a caern of the Wyld could not be maintained in New York City, and that the Bone Gnawers preserved the caern only by somehow changing it to a caern of fellowship and attracting a new totem (making the original totem subordinate).<br /> <br /> The best source about this is likely the second edition Players Guide to Werewolf which has the best section on caerns.<br /> <br /> One page 110, it states this:<br /> <br /> <i>If a sept were to abandon its caern, the site would waste away until it was virtually indistinguishable from the surrounding land, with only an increased potential there for possible future caerns. It takes hundreds of years for this diminishment to occur, so it is possible to reclaim a caern that has been abandoned within just the last few centuries.</i><br /> <br /> I do not think there is a canonical rite that closes down a caern. It just withers away until it does dormant. At some point the caern totem goes into slumber. However, I think it would be acceptable for there to be a Garou rite that respectfully &quot;shuts down&quot; the caern (that cannot be properly maintained) in order to prevent its possible future corruption or take over by the enemies of the Garou. It's always possible to reclaim the caern later, so you're not technically violating it. I imagine it is considered to be shameful among the Garou, but whether it inflicts a Renown loss may depend on the situation and the ST.<br /> <br /> Page 111 mentions a Rite of Reclamation (it is not described officially, but some mechanics are given for it) that assists the former caern totem into reactivating such a caern. But that is at the site of the original caern. I have never heard anything that describes a caern totem being &quot;transferred&quot; to a new caern location.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would rule if you want to create a new caern, you must perform the rite of caern building. You just can't transfer a slumbering caern totem spirit to someplace new.<br /> <br /> The sourcebook Guardians of the Caerns provides the most detail on caerns. It states that caern totems are themselves selected by Gaia according to the caern's purpose and other specifics, and it is not something that Garou can influence. I would consider it is possible that Gaia might awake an old caern totem and send it to the new caern. However, that is probably not typical, but it could be within the realm of possibility if the ST so wishes.<br /> <br /> I would also rule that it may be possible to detach the caern totem from an inactive caern so that devoted Garou can continue to interact with it. Its powers would drop to that of an ordinary spirit, and there would need to be lots of roleplay involved given the vastly changed circumstances. But there's nothing that inherently prevents that, it's just unlikely.<br /> <br /> I think this is definitely in the realm of ST fiat and judicious decision. The sourcebooks are not clear in this. But the above is how I would handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T06:03:19-07:00","id":1536620,"title":"","content":"Interesting situation, and I agree with everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said.<br /> <br /> We had a (somewhat) similar situation once where the players wanted to peacefully make a Spirit dormant again, and house-ruled that a Theurge with Rite of Spirit Awakening could use it to do so with increased difficulty. The argument was that knowledge of the Rite could be used to do the opposite, although that certainly doesn't work for every Rite. Perhaps it's possible to use the Rite of Reclamation in a similar way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T08:36:26-07:00","id":1536622,"title":"","content":"Fantastic summary of the rules as given, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, thank you as always. My take away will be as follows: the totem cannot be transferred, but there is a Renown-losing ritual that is traditionally used to seal a caern when the Garou must give it up. In this case, the actual physical space is going to be destroyed, so the chances of the Wyrm corrupting it are minimal, but the Garou will still opt to do so out of respect for the totem. They'll then be adrift in the city, with the leadership needing to hold the sept together as they hunt for a new site and prepare it for the creation of a new caern. I think I'll take a note from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> (thanks!) and have the rite be a more powerful and inverse version of the Rite of Spirit Awakening. <br /> <br /> Follow-up question: there's a Glass Walker Elder Theurge who wants to pragmatically steal the power of the caern before it's closed down to boost the spiritual batteries of his Weaver-aligned caern, allowing its portals to open at a greater distance and include more cities under its domain (it's a complicated story). What do you guys think about some means to siphon off a caern's power in such fashion? This Elder is heavily Weaver aligned, and since his initial request was rebuffed by the sept's garou, he's thinking of implanting a power-siphoning device or fetish or the like in the head of the huge drill that's boring out the tunnel that will pass through the caern's physical location. <br /> <br /> Does any of that resonate with existing mechanics or ideas put down in the books? Any thoughts on whether that's even feasible, in terms of stealing the caern's power to boost that of a massively Weaver-focused one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T13:26:28-07:00","id":1536636,"title":"","content":"Draining a caern is certainly a mechanic that exists- the first thing that came to mind was that it is the main reason why Garou don't like Mages around their caerns. An Awakened Mage or even a Sorcerer could absolutely make a Ritual that siphons power from one caern to another. If you have one of the Sorcerer supplements, you can take a look at Mana Manipulation (Quintessence Manipulation in the 20th Anniversary Edition). But it basically boils down to both being able to transfer 'energies' from on thing to another. Since Kinfolk have an affinity for sorcery, maybe a relative of the Glass Walker is in on it.<br /> <br /> I'm having a harder time thinking of examples from WtA. The BSDs would rather corrupt a caern than suck it dry and I don't remember any Rite to that effect. The closest match I can think of is the Ananasi's Rite of Weaving from their Breed Book. It's a Rite that lets them rewrite reality by manipulating the Great Web, so something like creating a power line between caerns would be well within the scope I would say. It's a really powerful Rite and specific to the Ananasi as beings especially close to the Weaver though, the Glass Walker would have to have a really good reason to know it (or have a Viskr ally to perform it for him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T14:54:00-07:00","id":1536645,"title":"","content":"Technically the Rite of Opened Caern taps the caern's power for use by one of its members, but this is with the permission of the caern spirit and regulated by the sept's pact with the caern totem and is limited in nature. There is also the infamous ritual in New Orleans By Night that the Gangrel Justicar uses to drain power from an abandoned caern. So it is theoretically possible provided the ST allows the creation or discovery of a new rite or other way to do so.<br /> <br /> However, in both of the above cases it's not like the power is permanently transferred. The person tapping the caern just gets a temporary boost of some sort. It's the difference between opening the water taps to fill your bottle and stealing the water from the reservoir to transfer it elsewhere. There's a magnitude difference. You would be literally ripping away part of the sacred power of the land and transplanting it elsewhere. Not impossible, but beyond the normal scope of how the Garou do things. That Garou would be treading new, perhaps dangerous and heretical, ground.<br /> <br /> I don't think other Garou would find the Glass Walker's plan acceptable. This would be a big scandal and crime if it was ever discovered. Furthermore, figuring out how to do such a thing likely takes a lot of time. Unless the Glass Walker knows well in advance that the caern will be closed, he may not have enough time to figure out how to do it. It's really up to you as ST if you want to allow something like that. And remember, once something can be done, it will be done multiple times. Do you really want this kind of power to exist in your chronicle?<br /> <br /> I'd most likely tell such a player that he cannot do such a thing like permanently transfer some power/rank from one caern to another. But I might allow him to temporarily transfer some kind of benefit provided that the player develop the rite/fetish in a way that I'd accept (provided there is enough time, but an elder theurge should be capable of it). I'd offer to work with the player to refine a good idea into something I'd accept, but I'd let him do all the heavy lifting to convince me. I wouldn't do his homework for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T22:38:03-07:00","id":1536661,"title":"","content":"The Mage route makes sense. Would just require my Elder GW to be in cahoots with the Technocracy, which isn't impossible. <br /> <br /> And you're right, Black Fox, the other Garou find the plan heinous and turn it down. The Elder GW is an NPC, so this would be more of a plot device to set up conflict that the PC's would have to make moral choices about. The tunnel would have been planned for the previous decade, so the GW would have had time, but...<br /> <br /> I think overall it only makes sense if Mages are involved, which in turn doesn't really make sense for the GW, who'd not invite them so intimately into the workings of a caern or trust them to actually transfer the power. I think I'll leave it at his having offered to explore the possibility, which left a really bad taste in the mouth of the traditional Garou, further widening the gap between them and the GW Sept.<br /> <br /> Still, thanks for helping me think this through, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T00:12:39-07:00","id":1536663,"title":"","content":"In case you want to preserve the plot line: It's possible that the totem of the GW sept's caern decided that one powerful active caern is better than two weak caerns, one of which is inactive. This would shift the conflict from directly between Garou to a conflict between Spirits. It's not like Gaian Spirits are all one happy family, and if it is between a Weaver and Wyld Spirit even less so. It would still depend on what kind of totems are involved, of course.<br /> <br /> So if it decided to consume the other caern's totem to absorb its power, it could have asked the GW elder to aid it in that. Perhaps to employ some minor Weaver Spirits with the Drain Gnosis Charm to nibble away at it. The whole thing becomes a bit more morally ambiguous for the Garou that way: they should be very familiar with the concept of the Strong consuming the Weak as a natural process. They probably still wouldn't like it very much, but at least it doesn't involve any outside parties like Mages. It also puts the GW elder in a bit less villainous light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T06:37:47-07:00","id":1536670,"title":"","content":"You also have the option to just house rule the rite.<br /> <br /> Fera don't have a rite to siphon a Caern that way simply because this is blasphemy for them, not because it can't be done. An NPC Elder that developed or found such a rite is far from farfetched.<br /> <br /> It is blasphemy. It's blasphemy even to the BSD. It is also the only good thing to do with a Caern that'll be utterly destroyed for no one's fault, the battle already lost. It is a profound disrespect with Gaia and also the only hope for a piece of their religion and valuable spiritual resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}